From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] DEBUG: PCI: qcom: runtime switch for the suspend memory floor

pcie_qcom.suspend_mem_floor (writable at runtime, default 1) lets a test
drop the suspend OPP to NULL like upstream, so the RPMh sleep set keeps
no DDR vote and the s2idle hang reproduces without rebuilding. Change it
only while the system is awake.

Not for shipping.
---
--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -2240,6 +2240,11 @@ static int qcom_pcie_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
  * during s2idle. Suspend-to-RAM tears the link down and keeps dropping
  * the OPP.
  */
+/* DEBUG: 0 drops the floor like upstream, to reproduce the no-vote s2idle hang. */
+static bool suspend_mem_floor = true;
+module_param(suspend_mem_floor, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(suspend_mem_floor, "Keep the suspend OPP DDR vote in s2idle (default: true)");
+
 static int qcom_pcie_set_suspend_opp(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 {
 	struct device *dev = pcie->pci->dev;
@@ -2247,7 +2252,7 @@ static int qcom_pcie_set_suspend_opp(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 	unsigned long freq;
 	int ret;
 
-	if (pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_MEM)
+	if (pm_suspend_target_state == PM_SUSPEND_MEM || !READ_ONCE(suspend_mem_floor))
 		return dev_pm_opp_set_opp(dev, NULL);
 
 	freq = dev_pm_opp_get_suspend_opp_freq(dev);
